<article class="env-lemma" id="04RB">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/04RB">Lemma <span data-tag="04RB">40.10.13</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $(U, R, s, t, c)$ be a groupoid scheme over $S$. Assume </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$U = \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(k)$ with $k$ a field, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$s, t$ are locally of finite type, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$R$ is reduced, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$k$ is perfect. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
  <p> Then $s, t : R \to U$ are smooth. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      By Lemma <a href="/tag/04R9" data-tag="04R9">40.4.1</a> the sheaf $\Omega _{R/U}$ is free. Hence the lemma follows from Varieties, Lemma <a href="/tag/04QP" data-tag="04QP">33.25.2</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>